{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/528475-dual-weilding","id":528475,"title":"Dual Weilding","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-25T21:11:18-07:00","id":528475,"title":"Dual Weilding","content":"Two pistols allow you to do more attacks in a round (and reduce recoil penalties if you using 2nd edition rules). So what's a point of melee dual wielding? Are there any bonuses? As i understand RAW there is +1 difficulty to offhand attacks, so if i have two swords i will use my main weapon every single strike. Did i miss something? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3799-zeitgeist","name":"Zeitgeist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T21:45:37-07:00","id":528521,"title":"","content":"Generally speaking in the cWOD rules in most editions... there really isn't a point to most dual wielding.<br /> <br /> For melee, the best use is to have something that offers a defensive bonus in you off hand like a shield or a parrying dagger. This usually gives you a better parry roll even with the off-hand penalty than not; or provides passive benefits in some of the systems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T23:34:02-07:00","id":528584,"title":"","content":"Boli Zousizhe have a Gift specifically geared toward using two weapons at once. Other than that, the only benefit is that you have another weapon ready if one gets knocked away or runs out of ammo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T03:48:08-07:00","id":528693,"title":"","content":"Dual weilding two guns does not give you extra attacks. You still have to use an action to actually attack. The main thing it does is that it looks cool and gives you more ammo... or even coincidentiality when you put out way too much ammou into the air <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T11:53:23-07:00","id":529082,"title":"","content":"Well, since guns have rates on them, you're maximum number of possible attacks is increased if you dual-wield them. If you use a gun with a rate of 3, that's 3 attacks regardless of how many you could pull off with your other stats. If you have two of them, it ups to 6 attacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T12:54:49-07:00","id":529141,"title":"","content":"I know that there are concerns other than realism, but I would invite anybody who thinks that using a pistol in each hand to be effective go out to a shooting range and try it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T14:33:56-07:00","id":529277,"title":"","content":"For a normal mortal, the system doesn't really make dual wield pistols all that appealing. If you're doing 20th split dice pools... even with 10 dice, cut between 4+ shots is highly ineffective. If you're doing the revised increasing penalties it is likewise pretty ineffective to bother.<br /> <br /> If you're a supernatural and have Celerity 5? Well being able to fire 6 times instead of 3 gets a ton more important.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T21:21:27-07:00","id":530641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/528475-dual-weilding?p=528693#post528693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dual weilding two guns does not give you extra attacks. You still have to use an action to actually attack. The main thing it does is that it looks cool and gives you more ammo... or even coincidentiality when you put out way too much ammou into the air <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It does. For example, Glock 17 max. 4 attacks in a round. Two Glocks - max. 8 attacks in a round.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/528475-dual-weilding?p=529277#post529277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For a normal mortal, the system doesn't really make dual wield pistols all that appealing. If you're doing 20th split dice pools... even with 10 dice, cut between 4+ shots is highly ineffective. If you're doing the revised increasing penalties it is likewise pretty ineffective to bother.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you use 20th edition rules then 8 attacks with 1 die each are better than 1 or 2 attacks with 8/4 dicepool in terms of DPS vs unarmored or light armored targets.<br /> <br /> IMO it's better to apply an offhand attack in the same initiative phase with the main hand (Dark Ages knife fighting style). In this scenario, dual weilding is more viable option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3799,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3799-zeitgeist","user":"Zeitgeist","date":". 05-28-2015, 12:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3799-zeitgeist","name":"Zeitgeist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T21:34:10-07:00","id":530651,"title":"","content":"Yeah if you have Celerity or something but are still limited by how fast the gun can recock and fire, having two pistols is a good idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T00:29:07-07:00","id":530729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zeitgeist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/528475-dual-weilding?p=530641#post530641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you use 20th edition rules then 8 attacks with 1 die each are better than 1 or 2 attacks with 8/4 dicepool in terms of DPS vs unarmored or light armored targets.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure the math on that is solid.<br /> <br /> For one thing, the odds of botching with eight 1 die attacks is pretty high (57%, 18% of that 57% will be botching more than once!); and you can't use WP safely. One early botch can easily remove the rest of your attacks.<br /> <br /> Another issue besides armor is going to be cover. If your target can get behind +2 diff cover, you're firing 4 shots at diff 8, and 4 shots at diff 9, all with one dice a piece. So it adds another facet of having to catch your target in the open for this to be effective.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T07:45:02-07:00","id":531007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zeitgeist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/528475-dual-weilding?p=530641#post530641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does. For example, Glock 17 max. 4 attacks in a round. Two Glocks - max. 8 attacks in a round.<br /> <br /> <br /> If you use 20th edition rules then 8 attacks with 1 die each are better than 1 or 2 attacks with 8/4 dicepool in terms of DPS vs unarmored or light armored targets.<br /> <br /> IMO it's better to apply an offhand attack in the same initiative phase with the main hand (Dark Ages knife fighting style). In this scenario, dual weilding is more viable option.</div> </div> </div> </div>It gives you extra rate of fire. That does not give you extra attacks. To get extra attacks you need to generate them through dicepool splitting or powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T02:09:36-07:00","id":540784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/528475-dual-weilding?p=531007#post531007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It gives you extra rate of fire. That does not give you extra attacks. To get extra attacks you need to generate them through dicepool splitting or powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes you are right. It's more legit statement.<br /> <br /> Can you tell me about multiple melee attacks in 2nd edition WoD storyteller system? There are multiple shots for firearms for sure (special rules at the combat section), but melee attacks confuse me a lot. If you look at weapons in VtM 2nd edition Players Guide you will see Double Strike Speciality for Knives. It allows you to split your dicepool and attack twice or more (+1 die and +1 difficulty to each attack). Does it mean you can't split die to gain multiple melee attacks without this speciality? Is it possible to attack 6 times if your melee dicepool is 6 by default?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3799,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3799-zeitgeist","user":"Zeitgeist","date":". 06-05-2015, 05:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3799-zeitgeist","name":"Zeitgeist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T06:17:09-07:00","id":541069,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure on the official rules, but I personally like to limit it to 'one attack per weapon, unless you have celerity/rage/other speed increaser', which makes dual wielding the only way for a human to get two attacks per round using both multiple actions and off-hand penalties (one with -1 die at difficulty 7, one with -2 dice at difficulty 9). This makes offensive dual wielding incredibly risky, but defensive dual wielding let's you attack normally and make a free parry (the same rules cover sword and shield in my games).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T13:47:56-07:00","id":541650,"title":"","content":"I usually use these rules<br /> <br /> Multiple attack (1 weapon)<br /> Divide dice pools, but the attacks are divided along the Initiative of the Character (i.e. Initiative 12, character makes 3 attacks, 1 at Initiative 12, 1 at initiative 8 and the last at initiative 4).<br /> <br /> Dual Weapons<br /> Divide dice pools, the two attacks are simoultaneous, +1 difficulty to the lesser hand (+2 if one weapon require a strong grip or precision, or the weapons are different).<br /> <br /> Dual Weapons with Ambidextrous Merit<br /> Divide dice pools, the two attacks are simoultaneous (+1 difficulty if one weapon require a strong grip or precision, or the weapons are different - no malus if Perception is at least 3).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}